<article class="project"><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--top">← Work</a><header class="project__hero"><div class="project__hero-media project__hero-media--shot"><a class="pshot pshot--link" href="https://github.com/Nizamohammed/Human_Gait_Analysis_LMPS-B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the Human Gait Analysis code on GitHub"><img src="/project/gait.jpg" alt="Human Gait Analysis"><span class="pshot__cue">View on GitHub</span></a></div><div class="project__hero-heading"><h1 class="project__title page-heading-reveal">Human Gait Analysis</h1><p class="project__hero-sub">Motion-sensor gait analysis at a robotics lab.</p><div class="project__hero-actions"><a class="project__hero-cta" href="https://github.com/Nizamohammed/Human_Gait_Analysis_LMPS-B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a></div></div></header><div class="project__meta project__meta--role"><span class="project__status"><span class="project__status-dot project__status-dot--done" aria-hidden="true"></span>Completed</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Dec 2022 to Feb 2023</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Research at RAL Lab</span></div><p class="project__role"><span class="project__role-label">Role</span>Lead machine learning researcher</p><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">About</p><div class="project__body"><p>Human Gait Analysis was a research project at DePaul's RAL Lab focused on translating raw motion-sensor signals into useful inputs for prosthetic locomotion. I built the data pipeline and the regression models that estimated limb position, direction, and speed from inertial and heading-reference sensors.</p></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Highlights</p><div class="project__body"><ul class="project__list"><li>Collected and standardized multichannel time-series signals from inertial motion and heading-reference sensors.</li><li>Built Python pipelines and visualizations for trajectories, speed, and joint motion to support gait-cycle inspection and sensor-quality checks.</li><li>Trained regression models to estimate limb position, direction, and speed from cleaned sensor signals.</li><li>Cut processing time by about 90% and improved processed data quality by about 30% versus the lab's initial manual workflow.</li></ul></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Stack</p><div class="project__body"><ul class="project__chips"><li class="project__chip">Python</li><li class="project__chip">NumPy</li><li class="project__chip">pandas</li><li class="project__chip">scikit-learn</li><li class="project__chip">Matplotlib</li></ul></div></section><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--bottom">← Work</a></article>
